  "id": "phonetics",
  "term": "phonetics",
  "definition": "Phonetics is the description and measurement of speech sounds, including how they are heard, transcribed, and examined with instrumental methods. In this context, it is used to study subtle features of speech production that may be missed by listening-based judgments alone.",
